// The Mosslight overworld: nine rooms in a 3x3 grid plus the dungeon vestibule. Geometry and doors
// were authored in phase 2; phase 3 added the first enemy spawns (see
// .autodev/phases/03-combat-enemies-determinism/PLAN.md). Phase 4 (see
// .autodev/phases/04-overworld-content/PLAN.md) makes the start room a cul-de-sac (its east/west
// doors and their reciprocals in south_shore/fallen_pines are removed), authors the sword, the
// lantern, three NPCs, the mill's step-plate puzzle, three secret chests off the main route, the
// lantern-locked dungeon entrance, and the room.sanctuary_gate stub the dungeon expands from in
// phase 5. Chests, NPCs and torches carved into a room's own dead corridor never share the
// room's other decorative tiles (water at (2..3, 3..4), the interior wall at (6, 6), bush at
// (18..19, 11..12)), so every alcove below reuses the same (18..22, 1..2) pocket regardless of
// which room it is authored in.
World(
    version: 1,
    start: (room: "room.lighthouse", spawn: "spawn.lighthouse.start"),
    route: (ember_required: false, home: "room.lighthouse", goal: "room.sanctuary_gate"),
    rooms: [
        (
